 "scribe_vocals_2": {
  "text": "Erythrocytes, red blood cells. Most abundant of all the cells in blood. Healthy adult man and on an average has five to five point five millions of RBCs per cubic millimeter. These formed in the red bone marrow. Nucleus devoid in most mammals. Biconcave in shape. Hemoglobin, iron containing complex protein. Red colored, hence the color, hence the name. Hemoglobin grams in every hundred ml, twelve to sixteen. Global transport of respiratory gas. Lifespan, one hundred twenty days. Destroyed in the spleen, graveyard of RBC. Hemoglobin, iron containing complex protein. Red colored, hence the color, hence the name. Erythrocytes, red blood cells.",
